aobj.c.inc and ftanim.c.inc are unchanged function excerpts from doldecomp/melee
(third_party/melee-decomp), under its MIT license. The source-verification test
compares both excerpts against the pinned submodule when present.

Only pure arithmetic is under test: FObj track dispatch, SRT transfer and
root-motion extraction are stubbed out in driver.c. Both original frame-clock
functions run, including FIRST_PLAY, stopped state, loop rewind, overshoot,
blend progress and Fighter remainder. No fusion was present in either function
in the NTSC-U 1.02 DOL (asm.py --fused); compile with -ffp-contract=off.
Finite inputs and positive loop spans use native fmodf, which has the same
finite remainder result as MSL. Invalid/NaN loop spans are outside this sweep.
